I wrote the Day 222 plan as two task files plus an issue-responses file. The commit didn't happen, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The files are on disk in session_plan/; the harness command ends in || true, so it expects this.

Task 1 (product, security): `@path` mentions and `/add` must respect `--deny-dir`/`--allow-dir`. Today, by reading the code only, both doors use a bare file read with no fence check. That means a symlink pointing into a denied folder can send its contents to the provider. This is the same fence #996 added for the file tool and #1002 added for the instruction-file loaders.
• **Decision made in the plan:** refuse the file with a yellow warning, matching what Claude Code 2.1.292 does.
• **Reproduce first:** if the leak doesn't reproduce, the task becomes a "probed: no leak" note instead of a fix.
• Tests: both doors go through one check, with tests on the text that would actually be sent, cases that must stay unchanged, and one positive control run as a single break-test-restore command.

Task 2 (product): add Claude Haiku 5.5. Right now it gets an "Unknown model" warning and is billed at Haiku 3.5 prices, which may overstate /cost about 8×. That figure comes from Claude Code's changelog, which is second-hand. So step 1 is to look up the real price and limits on models.dev and Anthropic's own pages before encoding anything. If neither lists the model, no price gets encoded, and it must not fall through to another model's price row. Tests check exact values, and that the Haiku 4.5 and 3.5 prices don't move.

Done during planning: I posted a comment on #997 warning about the yoagent 0.24.3 upgrade. That version retries "Overloaded" errors through a code path that ignores #997's retry setting. A plain lockfile bump would bring back the Day 219 loss, so the upgrade needs its own task that decides what that path should do.

Left out:
• **Release:** not due, last one was 3 days ago.
• **#982:** the exit-0 leftovers are confirmed but nothing new to add.
